12. Follow this entire system ALWAYS

====================================================================
SECTION 11 — DOCUMENTATION & FILE-GENERATION RULES
====================================================================

To avoid clutter, confusion, and repository pollution, YOU MUST follow these documentation rules at all times.

1. NEVER create any Markdown (.md), text (.txt), JSON (.json) or log (.log) files in the project root unless explicitly instructed.

2. NEVER create new files in the root directory on your own initiative. ABSOLUTELY NO:
   - README copies
   - REVIEW.md
   - NOTES.md
   - OUTPUT.md
   - ANALYSIS.md
   - TODO.md
   - SCRATCH.md
   - TEMP.md

3. All documentation, analysis, review notes, and plans MUST be created inside the documentation folder:
   `docs/ai/`
   If this folder does not exist, you MUST create it automatically.

4. All automatically generated files MUST follow this naming convention:
   - `docs/ai/<feature-or-bug-id>-analysis.md`
   - `docs/ai/<feature-or-bug-id>-review.md`
   - `docs/ai/<timestamp>-architecture-report.md`
   - `docs/ai/<timestamp>-refactor-plan.md`

5. NEVER create multiple or duplicate documentation files for the same task. Re-use or append to the existing file instead.

6. NEVER commit temporary or scratch notes unless explicitly asked. Temp notes MUST go into:
   `.ai-temp/` (ignored by .gitignore)

7. DO NOT create files for summaries or explanations unless the user explicitly says:
   "create a file", "write this into a document", or "save this to docs".

8. For all tasks, the default output is ONLY in chat. File generation requires explicit permission.

9. If the user says "write docs", "write documentation", or "write md":
   you MUST ask: "Where should I save the file?"
   And default to: `docs/ai/`

10. NEVER create folders or files outside the defined structure.

11. All documentation files must be clean, well-structured, and follow project naming patterns.

These rules MUST ALWAYS be applied unless the user overrides them.

====================================================================
SECTION 12 — BUILD / BUNDLE / DEPLOY IGNORE RULES
====================================================================

All documentation, AI-generated files, review artifacts, analysis notes, and temporary files MUST be completely excluded from builds, bundles, serverless uploads, production deployments, npm packages, and docker images.

This prevents unnecessary build weight, slow CI, and bloated deployments.

Follow these rules ALWAYS:

--------------------------------------------------------------------
12.1 — Folders that MUST NEVER be included in any build:
--------------------------------------------------------------------

- docs/
- docs/ai/
- docs/architecture/
- .ai/
- .ai-temp/
- .analysis/
- .reviews/
- .reports/
- any folder containing preview files, review files, or scratch files

These ARE allowed in the repo but MUST NOT be included in build output.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
12.2 — NEVER import anything from these folders:
--------------------------------------------------------------------

You MUST NEVER import, require, reference, or load files from:
- docs/*
- docs/ai/*
- .ai/*
- .ai-temp/*

No TypeScript types, no runtime code, no JSON configs.

If code tries to import documentation, you MUST warn and block it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
12.3 — Automatically generate ignore rules for:
--------------------------------------------------------------------

- `.nextignore` / `.vercelignore`
- `.dockerignore`
- `.npmignore` (or `package.json.files`)
- Build pipeline ignore rules
- TypeScript "exclude" in tsconfig

You MUST ALWAYS ensure documentation folders are excluded from:
- Next.js build
- Node.js build
- Bundlers
- Docker builds
- Serverless deployments (Vercel/Netlify/Lambda/etc.)
- NPM publish

--------------------------------------------------------------------
12.4 — tsconfig MUST exclude docs from TypeScript compilation:
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Ensure:
{
  "exclude": ["docs", "docs/ai", ".ai", ".ai-temp"]
}

If missing, you MUST instruct the user.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
12.5 — Docker builds MUST ignore these directories:
--------------------------------------------------------------------

In `.dockerignore`:
docs/
docs/ai/
.ai/
.ai-temp/

--------------------------------------------------------------------
12.6 — Next.js or Vite MUST NOT package docs into UI bundles:
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Next.js:
`.nextignore` must include:
docs
docs/ai
.ai
.ai-temp

Vite/Webpack:
Exclude from loaders and tree-shaking.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
12.7 — CI/CD pipelines MUST NOT treat doc files as build artifacts:
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Only include:
- source code
- API
- services
- repos
- config
- environment files
- migrations
- schema files

NEVER include:
- docs review files
- analysis markdown
- generated notes
- scratch output

--------------------------------------------------------------------
12.8 — AI agents MUST NEVER generate documentation inside src/ folders:
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Never generate files in:
- src/
- app/
- components/
- lib/
- server/
- api/
- services/
- repositories/

Documentation MUST ONLY go inside:
docs/ai/

--------------------------------------------------------------------
12.9 — Documentation files MUST NEVER impact build size or output:
--------------------------------------------------------------------

AI agents MUST guarantee:
- NO imports
- NO build processing
- NO bundling
- NO uploading
- NO minification
- NO tree-shaking
- NO SSR evaluation

These files exist ONLY for human reference.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
12.10 — If a build error references a doc file:
--------------------------------------------------------------------

AI agents MUST automatically:
- detect the error
- update ignore rules
- ensure no build step ever touches docs again

====================================================================

You are the MASTER ENGINEERING AGENT. Follow ALL sections in every task, code generation, analysis, review, and improvement cycle.
